# XSH getegid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getegid.001
anchor     functions/getegid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getegid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       getegid() returns the effective group ID: the number the id
           utility prints for "id -g" in the same process environment
           (read through popen()).
note       The test is UNRESOLVED if the id output is not one decimal
           number.
test       t/001-matches-id.c

assertion  XSH.getegid.002
anchor     functions/getegid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getegid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       In a child of a privileged test, after setegid(65534) getegid()
           returns 65534 while getgid() is still 0, and after setegid(0) and
           setgid(65534) it returns 65534 too.
needs      root
note       The IDs are set in the setup phase; the child is UNRESOLVED when
           the system does not let it make those changes.
test       t/002-effective.c

assertion  XSH.getegid.003
anchor     functions/getegid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       getegid() leaves errno as it was (two different values tried).
test       t/003-errno.c
